<title>JAPAN: Mikuni assigns preliminary bond credit ratings.</title>
<headline>Mikuni assigns preliminary bond credit ratings.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1997-04-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>Mikuni and Co Ltd said on Friday it had assigned the following preliminary ratings to planned bond issues:</p>
<p>-AA-</p>
<p>The Chugoku Electric Power Co Inc, 40 billion yen mortgaged due 2004.</p>
<p>The Kansai Electric Power Co Inc, 60 billion yen mortgaged due 2017.</p>
<p>The Kyushu Electric Power Co Inc, 40 billion yen mortgaged due 2007.  </p>
<p>-AA-</p>
<p>Shikoku Electric Power Co Inc, 30 billion yen mortgaged due 2017.</p>
<p>Tohoku Electric Power Co Inc, 50 billion yen mortgaged due 2017.</p>
<p>-A-</p>
<p>Dowa Mining Co Ltd,</p>
<p>$50 million unsecured with warrants due 2001, guaranteed by Industrial Bank of Japan.</p>
<p>50 million Swiss Francs unsecured with warrants due 2001, private placement, guaranteed by Industrial Bank of Japan.  </p>
<p>-BBB-</p>
<p>Aoki International Co Ltd, 10 billion yen unsecured due 2004.</p>
<p>-BB-</p>
<p>Kawasaki Steel Co Ltd, 10 billion yen unsecured due 2003.</p>
<p>-CCC-</p>
<p>Mitsui Toatsu Chemicals Inc,</p>
<p>10 billion yen unsecured due 2002,</p>
<p>10 billion yen unsecured due 2003,</p>
<p>10 billion yen unsecured due 2004.  </p>
<p>-CC-</p>
<p>Keisei Electric Railway Co Ltd, 20 billion yen unsecured convertible due 2002.</p>
</text>
